# obsidian-llm-wiki — external acquire-skill bin overrides (OPTIONAL).
# =============================================================================
# You normally DON'T need this file. `wiki-import` AUTO-DISCOVERS the external
# acquire skills (html / pdf / pptx / transcript-fetcher) across your harness's
# skills dir (any `~/.<harness>/skills` — Claude Code, pi, codex, …), and
# `bin/install-globally.sh` writes the resolved paths to the LIVE copy at:
#
#     ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/obsidian-llm-wiki/skills.env
#
# which the wiki-* CLIs auto-load at startup (no manual `source` needed).
#
# Copy this file to that path (or just export the vars in your shell) ONLY to
# PIN or OVERRIDE a skill that lives off the standard path:
#
#     mkdir -p ~/.config/obsidian-llm-wiki
#     cp config/skills.env.example ~/.config/obsidian-llm-wiki/skills.env
#     # then uncomment + edit the WIKI_*_BIN line(s) you need
#
# Resolution precedence, highest first:
#
#   --<flag> CLI arg  >  $WIKI_<BIN> in your shell  >  skills.env  >
#   dynamic <harness>/skills discovery  >  PATH  >  DEPENDENCY_MISSING
#
# Each var points at the skill's entry SCRIPT (invoked via python3). Uncomment
# and edit only the ones you need; leave the rest to auto-discovery.
# =============================================================================

# URL / HTML → clean markdown (reader extraction; the `html` skill).
# On pi this skill's dir is named `html2md` — point at wherever yours lives:
# WIKI_HTML_BIN="$HOME/.claude/skills/html/scripts/html2md.py"

# The SAME `html` skill, but its VERB LAUNCHER (TASK 072). WIKI_HTML_BIN above points at
# `scripts/html2md.py`, a thin shim with no verb routing; the verbs (`fetch`/`md`/`get`) live on
# the extensionless `scripts/html`. `wiki-import` needs the `get` verb because it is the only
# door into the skill's SSRF-guarded fetch ladder — the two URL-fetch call sites go through it
# instead of a bare urlopen. Pin this ONLY if auto-discovery finds the wrong launcher.
#   Requires an `html` build whose `--help` lists `html get URL`; older builds are REFUSED with
#   DEPENDENCY_MISSING rather than silently falling back to an unguarded fetch.
# WIKI_HTML_LAUNCHER_BIN="$HOME/.claude/skills/html/scripts/html"

# PDF → text (the `pdf` skill).
# WIKI_PDF_EXTRACT_BIN="$HOME/.claude/skills/pdf/scripts/pdf_extract.py"

# Office (docx / pptx / xlsx) → text via the hardened LibreOffice wrapper.
# WIKI_SOFFICE_WRAPPER="$HOME/.claude/skills/pptx/scripts/_soffice.py"

# Video URL → transcript (the `transcript-fetcher` skill).
# WIKI_TRANSCRIPT_BIN="$HOME/.claude/skills/transcript-fetcher/scripts/fetch.py"

# .vtt / .srt caption de-timestamper (also from `transcript-fetcher`).
# WIKI_VTT_CLEANER="$HOME/.claude/skills/transcript-fetcher/scripts/sources/_vtt_to_text.py"

# --- Alternatively: add extra roots for discovery instead of per-bin pins ---
# os.pathsep-separated list of skill roots to scan FIRST (e.g. a shared/system
# install). Discovery still falls back to the per-harness dirs afterward.
# WIKI_SKILLS_DIRS="/opt/acquire-skills:$HOME/custom/skills"
